# RME invoice correction & receipt versioning — foundation (rule 190)

Evidence: `docs/sprints/feature-rme-invoice-correction-receipt-foundation-1.md`.
Builds on rule 188 (audit) and rule 189 (Phase 0 prerequisites). Where this rule and
those disagree about what EXISTS, this rule is newer.

Labels: **CURRENT_PRODUCTION_BEHAVIOR** (true on production after this release),
**IMPLEMENTED_THIS_RELEASE** (code exists, may be dormant behind the flag),
**PROPOSED** (design only — never cite as behaviour), **PENDING_OWNER_DECISION**.

## 1. What production does after this release — CURRENT_PRODUCTION_BEHAVIOR
1. The flag `rme.invoice_correction` (env `FEATURE_RME_INVOICE_CORRECTION`, risk
   `critical`) ships **OFF**. With it off, every correction mutation route answers
   **404** (including through its FormRequest, so a malformed POST cannot reveal the
   endpoint), and every service mutation refuses independently.
2. The three operational permissions — `request_rme_invoice_correction`,
   `approve_rme_invoice_correction`, `apply_rme_invoice_correction` — are seeded and
   granted to **NO role** (Super Admin holds them only through its wildcard). Turning
   the flag on therefore still enables nobody until an owner grants a role.
3. Invoice pages, receipts, payments and reports are **byte-identical** to before
   while the flag is off and nothing was corrected: the cashier correction panel
   runs no query in that state.
4. The read-only oversight area **Billing Correction** (Daftar Pasien Koreksi,
   Riwayat & Detail Koreksi) exists for `Finance Klinik` and `Data Analyst` via the
   fifth oversight permission `view_billing_correction_oversight` (rule 186 §2). It
   shows history; with no correction ever made it is empty.

## 2. Correction model — IMPLEMENTED_THIS_RELEASE
5. **Only PRE-PAYMENT corrections exist.** An invoice that is not `UNPAID`, has any
   payment row, belongs to a cancelled visit, or produced a lab case candidate (D23)
   is refused with a stable `[CODE]`. Post-payment is a declared type that is NOT
   enabled (`RmeInvoiceCorrectionType::ENABLED`).
6. Lifecycle `SUBMITTED → APPROVED → APPLIED`, plus `REJECTED`, `CANCELLED`, `STALE`
   (all terminal). Only `SUBMITTED`/`APPROVED` are active, and **at most one active
   correction per invoice** — enforced by a partial unique index
   (`trx_rme_inv_corr_one_active_uq`) and the invoice row lock.
7. **Maker ≠ checker is enforced in the SERVICE under the row lock**, never only in
   the policy: `Gate::before` lets Super Admin pass every policy, so the policy
   cannot stop a Super Admin approving their own request. Refused attempts are
   audited as `RME_INVOICE_CORRECTION_REFUSED` after rollback.
8. **Lock order: invoice row first, then the correction row** — the same lock every
   payment path takes. Apply re-reads the invoice under that lock and marks the
   correction **STALE** (persisted, then refused) when a payment landed, the status,
   version or content changed, or lab candidates appeared. Never move the staleness
   checks before the lock: PostgreSQL concurrency test 1 kills that mutant.
9. Totals are **recomputed server-side in integer cents**. Submitted totals, branch,
   patient, visit and invoice ids are never trusted. The applied total must equal
   the approved total or the whole apply rolls back (`LogicException`).
10. **No Rp0 bypass.** A correction can never create a zero line or a zero/negative
    invoice total. A pre-existing zero line kept unchanged is not new.
11. Price authority (D21) is NOT invented: a changed line uses the same active
    treatment / doctor / non-negative / discount-≤-gross rules as invoice creation.
11a. An existing item's treatment may be changed to another ACTIVE treatment but
    never cleared, and an existing item's **doctor is never re-attributed** (doctor
    income attribution is undecided policy). The form always offers an item's current
    treatment, even if deactivated, so an untouched line can never become a change.
11b. The approver (cashier detail, oversight detail and print) always sees original
    → proposed treatment AND doctor on every line, with a treatment change marked —
    approval is never blind to a non-money change.
11c. Overflow is refused before multiplying; an invoice whose total is already
    negative is refused with a stable code (never pushed into a CHECK constraint).
12. Reviewed content of a correction, its lines and events is **immutable** at the
    model layer; deletes are refused. Only lifecycle columns move.

## 3. Receipts and document versions — IMPLEMENTED_THIS_RELEASE
13. On first apply the original invoice document is frozen as **v0 ORIGINAL**
    (snapshot schema v1 + SHA-256); every apply then freezes **vN REVISION** linked to
    its correction. `trx_rme_invoice_document_versions` rows are immutable.
14. A frozen version is rendered **only from its snapshot**, never from live rows.
15. Snapshots carry no patient name, Nomor RM or KTP/NIK — identity stays on the
    patient record. Audit payloads carry ids, codes, cents and `reason_length` only.
16. A revised invoice's printed document shows "Versi Dokumen: Revisi ke-N". Because
    only UNPAID invoices are correctable, **no issued receipt is ever invalidated**.

## 4. Oversight — IMPLEMENTED_THIS_RELEASE
17. Billing Correction routes are **GET-only**, gated by
    `view_billing_correction_oversight`; print/PDF/CSV additionally need
    `export_oversight_data`. Out of oversight branch scope answers **404**.
18. The oversight roles gain **no** correction mutation permission, and the
    laboratory `Finance` role gains nothing.

## 4a. Known residual — PENDING_OWNER_DECISION (D10)

> **SUPERSEDED IN PART by rule 191 (ACTIVATION-RME-INVOICE-CORRECTION-PREPAYMENT-1).**
> The residual below is CLOSED: every payment path now binds the form to each
> settled invoice's `correction_version` under the invoice row lock. The reasoning
> that it "depends on D10" was too broad — D10 asks whether a PENDING correction
> blocks payment; binding to an APPLIED change is required under either answer.
> D10 itself is still PENDING. Text kept as the record of what was true at release.

18a. A payment form is not bound to the invoice `correction_version`: if a correction
    is applied while a cashier has the payment page open, the payment settles against
    the corrected total. The correction side is safe (a payment that lands first makes
    it STALE); binding the payment to the version changes the payment path and
    depends on D10. It cannot happen while the flag is OFF.

## 5. Not implemented — PENDING_OWNER_DECISION
19. Never report as active: post-payment correction, refund, payment reversal,
    patient credit balance, retroactive revenue adjustment, Rp0 adjustment, financial
    settlement. Owner decisions D1–D27 were all **PENDING** at release; the feature
    stays OFF until D1 (approval authority), D10 (pending correction vs payment),
    D21 (price authority) and D7 (receipt versioning policy) are decided.
20. Enabling the flag is a separate, owner-approved operational act — never a side
    effect of a deploy, a seeder or another sprint.

## 6. Regression requirements
21. Suites `tests/Feature/RmeInvoiceCorrection/*` are declared in
    `config/ci_runner.php` `critical_gate_mandatory_suites` and selected by the
    `RmeInvoiceCorrection` token in BOTH critical-gate variants.
22. The concurrency suite needs PostgreSQL row locks and uses a child PHP process to
    hold the competing transaction; it skips on SQLite and executes in CI (PG 16).
